From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11.drv: Promote managed owners across threads asynchronously.

AI-assisted (Claude, Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted
upstream.

Avoids a deadlock between threads (the SOLIDWORKS simulation mesh
stalled).

Header added on 2026-11-11, before winum-11.20-1 (the patch body is
unchanged). Problem, cause, Windows behaviour and validation:
docs/patches/winex11-owner-managed-async.md.

--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -1206,7 +1206,10 @@
     if (!(owner = NtUserGetWindowRelative( hwnd, GW_OWNER ))) return;
     if (is_managed( owner )) return;
 
-    NtUserSetWindowPos( owner, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, flags );
+    /* The owner thread may be waiting for this window to finish creation. */
+    NtUserSetWindowPos( owner, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0,
+                        flags | (NtUserGetWindowThread( owner, NULL ) != GetCurrentThreadId()
+                                 ? SWP_ASYNCWINDOWPOS : 0) );
 }
 
 
